# verify-contract.mjs used a raw NUL byte as a path sentinel (c137/c144), which made
# git classify it as binary and render its PRs as unreviewable "Bin" blobs - the one
# file whose job is to stop a gate passing vacuously was itself unreviewable. The NUL is
# now escaped (\\u0000) so this is defensive, but keep it: it forces a text diff even if
# a NUL sentinel is ever reintroduced, and keeps the security-critical checker reviewable.
app-mobile/scripts/verify-contract.mjs text diff
